CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*lsm_oinfo[0])...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct lov_oinfo)...)
#65: FILE: drivers/staging/lustre/lustre/obdecho/echo_client.c:486:
+	(*lsmp)->lsm_oinfo[0] = kzalloc(sizeof(struct lov_oinfo), GFP_NOFS);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

